==Strategy==
This level is just pure DPS spam, so it's best to fight spam with spam. Use your stackable area attackers like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]. Thanks to the two Kang Roos at the start, you can kill them and stall until you have full money, then just start your attack.

This stage only becomes threatening on {{3c}}, where every enemy is boosted enough to where your Erasers will barely hold up. Because of this, you should aim to abuse the starting Ottas to stack up damage, and then kill everything on base hit. Using the [[Cat Cannon]] to sync up the Capies is also extremely important, because they will kill everything in just one hit on {{3c}}, even a Lv.50 [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]!

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: While you can get away with not using them on {{1c}}, on higher difficulties, Stone Cat is necessary to win. No other Cat can withstand the insane combined DPS of the Otta-smack-us, Dark Otters, Shadow Boxer Ks AND Capies at once. Boosting them to Lv.50 is also extremely recommended, as the threats has potential to deal over 500k damage in just a second, melting through your poor rock.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza Cat has massive damage against [[Dark Enemies|Dark]], and can also fire off [[Wave Attack]]s through [[Talents]], both extending his reach and doubling his already good damage. His slow Talent can also help to stall the enemies for just a little longer.
*[[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Flying Cat]]: Brainwashed Flying has a 100% chance to slow Traitless with 100% uptime on top of having already-great damage output. They can hold back the hordes of Otta-smack-us easily, but they are vulnerable to being killed by Dark Otters due to their higher range.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: Jagando has guaranteed knockback on his last hit, as well as having great damage output, both of which will help to keep the Ottas at bay.

==Trivia==
*Concrete Ocean may be a reference to [[jojowiki:Stone_Ocean|Stone Ocean]] of [[wikipedia:JoJo's Bizarre Adventure|Jojo's Bizarre Adventure]], the 6th chapter of the ongoing series published in the [[wikipedia:Weekly Shonen Jump (American magazine)|Weekly Shonen Jump]] by [[wikipedia:Hirohiko Araki|Hirohiko Araki]].

